# Update the core of a Draft, and print its draftId, threadId, url and attachments as JSON
# The Draft keeps its attachments, and is never sent. The url opens it in Gmail
# The draftId is printed by gmail-draft-create, gmail-draft-read and gmail-thread-read
# A flag that is absent keeps the current value. Pass at least one flag
# Flags:
# --to <address>       New recipient
# --subject <text>     New subject
# --body <text>        New body, sent as text/plain
# --body-file <path>   New body read from a file. A .md file is also sent as HTML
#                      Pass one of --body or --body-file, never both
# --account <name>     Account of the Draft. The default account if empty
# Each attachment has partId, filename, mimeType and size, never its bytes
# Gmail gives new partId values to the attachments, so read them in the output
# Usage:
# $ gmail-draft-update draftId --subject "New subject"
# $ gmail-draft-update draftId --to a@b.c --body "New body"
# $ gmail-draft-update draftId --body-file ./body.md --account perso
setopt local_options err_return

local libDir="${functions_source[$0]:A:h:h}/__lib"
node "${libDir}/bin/gmail-draft-update.js" "$@"
